\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces \texttt  {\small  movcavlinfs} coupled evolution under \texttt  {\small  linfs} (compare Fig.~8 / \texttt  {\small  movcav34} zstar). (a) The moving mesh: node and cavity-node counts per increment, with nodes added/removed; the increment shrinks and the cavity is preserved. (b) PISM ice volume and floating area. (c) FESOM cavity-mean and total melt --- stable in the observed circum-Antarctic range, no escalation.}}{21}{figure.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:linfs-evo}{{13}{21}{\code {movcavlinfs} coupled evolution under \code {linfs} (compare Fig.~8 / \code {movcav34} zstar). (a) The moving mesh: node and cavity-node counts per increment, with nodes added/removed; the increment shrinks and the cavity is preserved. (b) PISM ice volume and floating area. (c) FESOM cavity-mean and total melt --- stable in the observed circum-Antarctic range, no escalation}{figure.13}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces The open-cavity fill fix. (a) A newly-iced column: carrying its open-ocean water (red) puts $+6.6$\,\textdegree {}C at the ice base; the freezing cap (blue) over-cools the deep column; seeding from the nearest existing cavity (green) gives a real cold ice-shelf-water profile with the deep column intact. (b) Ice-base thermal driving $T-T_f$ over the 182 open$\to $cavity columns after cavity-seeding --- almost all near freezing; the nine circled ($>0$\,\textdegree {}C) are physical warm-cavity donors.}}{22}{figure.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:newlyiced}{{14}{22}{The open-cavity fill fix. (a) A newly-iced column: carrying its open-ocean water (red) puts $+6.6$\,\textdegree {}C at the ice base; the freezing cap (blue) over-cools the deep column; seeding from the nearest existing cavity (green) gives a real cold ice-shelf-water profile with the deep column intact. (b) Ice-base thermal driving $T-T_f$ over the 182 open$\to $cavity columns after cavity-seeding --- almost all near freezing; the nine circled ($>0$\,\textdegree {}C) are physical warm-cavity donors}{figure.14}{}}
